  "gapAssignments": [],
  "finalCues": [
    {
      "verse": 1,
      "text": "Then Job replied:",
      "start": 2.105,
      "end": 3.35
    },
    {
      "verse": 2,
      "text": "“If only my anguish could be weighed and all my misery be placed on the scales!",
      "start": 3.731,
      "end": 9.079
    },
    {
      "verse": 3,
      "text": "It would surely outweigh the sand of the seas— no wonder my words have been impetuous.",
      "start": 9.8,
      "end": 15.81
    },
    {
      "verse": 4,
      "text": "The arrows of the Almighty are in me, my spirit drinks in their poison; God’s terrors are marshaled against me.",
      "start": 16.14,
      "end": 24.72
    },
    {
      "verse": 5,
      "text": "Does a wild donkey bray when it has grass, or an ox bellow when it has fodder?",
      "start": 25.32,
      "end": 30.618
    },
    {
      "verse": 6,
      "text": "Is tasteless food eaten without salt, or is there flavor in the sap of the mallow ?",
      "start": 30.94,
      "end": 37.159
    },
    {
      "verse": 7,
      "text": "I refuse to touch it; such food makes me ill.",
      "start": 37.8,
      "end": 42.02
    },
    {
      "verse": 8,
      "text": "“Oh, that I might have my request, that God would grant what I hope for,",
      "start": 42.611,
      "end": 47.0
    },
    {
      "verse": 9,
      "text": "that God would be willing to crush me, to let loose his hand and cut off my life!",
      "start": 47.02,
      "end": 52.52
    },
    {
      "verse": 10,
      "text": "Then I would still have this consolation— my joy in unrelenting pain— that I had not denied the words of the Holy One.",
      "start": 53.08,
      "end": 63.719
    },
    {
      "verse": 11,
      "text": "“What strength do I have, that I should still hope? What prospects, that I should be patient?",
      "start": 64.78,
      "end": 72.45
    },
    {
      "verse": 12,
      "text": "Do I have the strength of stone? Is my flesh bronze?",
      "start": 72.56,
      "end": 77.38
    },
    {
      "verse": 13,
      "text": "Do I have any power to help myself, now that success has been driven from me?",
      "start": 77.42,
      "end": 83.179
    },
    {
      "verse": 14,
      "text": "“Anyone who withholds kindness from a friend forsakes the fear of the Almighty.",
      "start": 84.381,
      "end": 89.59
    },
    {
      "verse": 15,
      "text": "But my brothers are as undependable as intermittent streams, as the streams that overflow",
      "start": 89.98,
      "end": 96.52
    },
    {
      "verse": 16,
      "text": "when darkened by thawing ice and swollen with melting snow,",
      "start": 96.52,
      "end": 100.5
    },
    {
      "verse": 17,
      "text": "but that stop flowing in the dry season, and in the heat vanish from their channels.",
      "start": 100.5,
      "end": 107.12
    },
    {
      "verse": 18,
      "text": "Caravans turn aside from their routes; they go off into the wasteland and perish.",
      "start": 107.98,
      "end": 113.5
    },
    {
      "verse": 19,
      "text": "The caravans of Tema look for water, the traveling merchants of Sheba look in hope.",
      "start": 113.7,
      "end": 119.45
    },
    {
      "verse": 20,
      "text": "They are distressed, because they had been confident; they arrive there, only to be disappointed.",
      "start": 119.86,
      "end": 125.459
    },
    {
      "verse": 21,
      "text": "Now you too have proved to be of no help; you see something dreadful and are afraid.",
      "start": 126.02,
      "end": 132.58
    },
    {
      "verse": 22,
      "text": "Have I ever said, ‘Give something on my behalf, pay a ransom for me from your wealth,",
      "start": 132.82,
      "end": 138.799
    },
    {
      "verse": 23,
      "text": "deliver me from the hand of the enemy, rescue me from the clutches of the ruthless’?",
      "start": 139.0,
      "end": 143.779
    },
    {
      "verse": 24,
      "text": "“Teach me, and I will be quiet; show me where I have been wrong.",
      "start": 144.64,
      "end": 150.379
    },
    {
      "verse": 25,
      "text": "How painful are honest words! But what do your arguments prove?",
      "start": 151.0,
      "end": 156.459
    },
    {
      "verse": 26,
      "text": "Do you mean to correct what I say, and treat my desperate words as wind?",
      "start": 157.04,
      "end": 161.939
    },
    {
      "verse": 27,
      "text": "You would even cast lots for the fatherless and barter away your friend.",
      "start": 162.24,
      "end": 166.699
    },
    {
      "verse": 28,
      "text": "“But now be so kind as to look at me. Would I lie to your face?",
      "start": 167.18,
      "end": 173.139
    },
    {
      "verse": 29,
      "text": "Relent, do not be unjust; reconsider, for my integrity is at stake.",
      "start": 173.8,
      "end": 179.679
    },
    {
      "verse": 30,
      "text": "Is there any wickedness on my lips? Can my mouth not discern malice?",
      "start": 180.92,
      "end": 187.2
    }
  ],
